This Software includes an Android Device Administrator receiver and an
Accessibility Service that are specifically designed to resist casual
removal, deactivation, or uninstallation of the Software (a "self-control"
or "commitment device" mechanism). By installing, distributing, or using
this Software, you additionally agree to the following:

1. SELF-INSTALLATION AND CONSENT ONLY
   This Software is intended to be installed by a person on a device that
   person owns and controls, as a voluntary personal commitment tool. It is
   NOT intended, licensed, or authorized to be installed on any device
   belonging to, or primarily used by, another person without that person's
   full knowledge, understanding, and freely given consent to its
   anti-removal behavior. Installing this Software on another adult's
   device without their informed consent, or on a minor's device as a
   covert monitoring tool, may violate computer-fraud, wiretapping,
   stalkerware, or consumer-protection laws in your jurisdiction. The
   authors and contributors expressly disclaim any license, permission, or
   endorsement to use this Software in that manner.

2. NO GUARANTEE OF EFFECTIVENESS
   The Software filters and restricts access using DNS-level and
   accessibility-level controls on the device. These mechanisms have known
   limitations (e.g., alternate DNS/VPN configuration, factory reset,
   sideloaded tools, or OS updates that change API behavior) and can be
   bypassed by a sufficiently motivated user, including the installing
   user. The Software makes no representation or warranty that it will
   successfully block any specific content, site, or behavior at any time.

3. NOT A MEDICAL OR THERAPEUTIC DEVICE
   This Software is a personal productivity/self-control tool. It is not a
   medical device, is not a substitute for professional treatment,
   counseling, or therapy, and makes no clinical claim to treat, cure, or
   prevent any behavioral or mental health condition. Anyone seeking help
   for compulsive behavior is encouraged to consult a licensed professional.

4. ASSUMPTION OF RISK FOR DEVICE-LEVEL PERMISSIONS
   Device Administrator and Accessibility Service permissions grant
   elevated control over the device (e.g., resisting uninstall, observing
   on-screen UI events to detect attempts to disable the app). Users
   granting these permissions do so at their own risk and are solely
   responsible for understanding what the permissions allow before granting
   them. The removal flow (PIN + timed delay) is the only sanctioned way to
   disable these permissions through the app itself.

5. LIABILITY
   To the maximum extent permitted by law, in addition to the MIT
   warranty/liability disclaimer above, the authors and contributors are
   not liable for any lockout, data loss, device malfunction, relationship
   or workplace consequence, or other harm arising from installation,
   misuse, or inability to remove this Software.

If you plan to distribute this Software publicly (e.g., via an app store),
you are responsible for ensuring your listing, in-app disclosures, and
permission justifications comply with that platform's policies
(particularly around Accessibility API use and anti-uninstall behavior)
and with the laws of the jurisdictions where it will be available.
